<% content_for :title, "Demo access, Papi" %>
<% content_for :description, "How to get into Papi: a shared demo login, or an account made by hand. There is no public signup." %>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
  <h1 class="display text-[34px] tracking-tight">Demo access</h1>

  <div class="prose mt-8">
    <p>
      Papi has no signup page, and that is deliberate. It is a small tool run on a
      small server, and accounts are made by hand.
    </p>

    <h2>The demo login</h2>
    <p>
      Three accounts share one group and one project, so you can watch a spec change
      move through review: propose it as one person, comment and approve as another.
      The project arrives with an open candidate that already carries a thread and an
      approval, so there is something to read the moment you log in. Everything is
      reset overnight, so nothing you do there is precious.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded border border-slate-400 bg-slate-50 p-6">
    <div class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-600">Demo logins</div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      Not open yet. The three accounts land with the first public deploy, and their
      credentials appear here.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-10">
    <h2>An account of your own</h2>
    <p>
      The demo group is a sandbox and is wiped nightly. If you want a project that
      keeps its history, ask, and one gets made for you.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
